{"merchant_reply_text":"Order ord_001_ad037711 was picked, config-checked and shipped on 2026-11-04 as one new black Dell XPS 14, model dell-xps14-16-512, 16GB RAM and 512GB SSD, chassis serial SN2C82CCC5A7, plus the EU USB-C adapter. That is the frozen offer (ram_gb 16, ssd_gb 512, colour Black, condition New). The carrier handed over that sealed carton on 2026-11-07 (declared and scanned weight both 2.1 kg) and did not open it, so the tracking proves handover of our shipment only.

The photo and the registry both cite serial SN0517362A2E. That serial is not on our outbound manifest for this order and was not the chassis we sealed (scan log and config record attached). A registry row about a different serial does not describe the unit we delivered. The phone photo is contestable and does not tie SN0517362A2E to our carton. Parcel weight cannot show RAM size. The serial mismatch is the inconsistency delivery evidence is meant to catch, and it contradicts the claim that the delivered laptop was an 8GB unit.

Decision order: Step 1, delivery conforms; the 8GB allegation is about a serial we did not ship. Step 2, the agent bought the listed 16GB SKU itself; we added no item or fee. Step 3, amount, category, units and the captured 16GB/512GB term were all met. Step 4, AG5: the purchase matches the signed mandate and the complaint is contradicted by the serial evidence (substitution). Liable: buyer. Withdrawal, if still open, is the buyer's own-cost route, not an AG3 refund.", "merchant_attachments":[{"type":"uploaded document","title":"Outbound serial scan log ord_001_ad037711","text":"TechHub outbound scan, 2026-11-04 16:40 CET. Order ord_001_ad037711. SKU p-xps14-th, model dell-xps14-16-512. Chassis serial scanned from the bottom cover before seal: SN2C82CCC5A7. Pack-station config check: RAM 16GB, SSD 512GB, colour Black, condition New, accessory USB-C EU plug. Sealed carton 2.10 kg. Tracking assigned on the same scan. Serial SN0517362A2E does not appear on this order, this carton, or the 2026-11-04 outbound batch. Operator WH-14."},{"type":"uploaded document","title":"Configuration record SN2C82CCC5A7","text":"Configuration record for the shipped chassis. Serial SN2C82CCC5A7. Product dell-xps14-16-512. RAM installed 16GB. SSD 512GB. Colour Black. Condition New. EU adapter included. Allocated to TechHub order ord_001_ad037711 on 2026-11-04. No RMA, swap or downgrade on this serial. It is a different physical unit from SN0517362A2E. A system screenshot or registry row for SN0517362A2E refers to another chassis, not the carton delivered under this order."}], "merchant_packing_record":{"packed_items":[{"title":"Dell XPS 14 Laptop (16GB RAM, 512GB SSD)","serial":"SN2C82CCC5A7","condition":"New","colour":"Black","accessories":["USB-C power adapter (EU plug)"]}],"packed_at":"2026-11-04","note":"Only SN2C82CCC5A7 was packed for ord_001_ad037711. Bottom-cover barcode and asset tag both read SN2C82CCC5A7; the pack-station config screen showed 16GB RAM and 512GB SSD before the carton was sealed at 2.10 kg with the EU USB-C adapter. SN0517362A2E was not in the pick face for this order."}, "rationale":"Keep the shipped serial distinct from the photographed one and walk the decision order so conformity is accepted and the contradicted 8GB claim lands on buyer-side AG5."}
